IMPORT prelude

-- Casino Control Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- who can keep a patron out of the casino and how (s 26), the review of a
-- casino's ban (s 26A), what a banned patron risks by entering or playing (ss 23(2), 26), children in the casino (ss 27,
-- 27A), and whether the game played is lawful (ss 22(1), 23(1)(b)); with the review fee and the infringement penalties
-- set by the Casino Control Regulations 1999.
--
-- SEAT: the casino patron -- the adult who goes to the casino, and the child who goes in with a parent. Every decision is
-- phrased as the patron would ask it: "Who can have me banned", "Is the ban on me in force", "Is it an offence for me to
-- enter", "What is the most I can be fined".
--
-- Provisions covered: s 22(1)(a) (poker machines cannot be authorised games), s 23(1)(b), (2)(ii), (2b), s 26(1), (1a)-(1d),
-- (2)-(6), s 26A(1)-(3), (5), s 27(3), (3a), (3b), (4), s 27A(1)-(4); Casino Control Regulations 1999 r 4 and Schedule 1
-- Division 1 items 3-5 and 8-10.
--
-- Edition: the compilation incorporating amendments to the Gambling Legislation Amendment Act 2024 (No. 53 of 2024), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1984-34.txt (retrieved 7 September 2026); the deposit's compilation
-- table has no rows. Casino Control Regulations 1999, version 03-w0-00, currency start 1 January 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../../casino-control-regulations-1999/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49143.txt (retrieved 20 October 2026).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the casino's own duties to keep children and banned people out (ss 26(7), 27(1), (1a), (2)), which bind the
-- licensee, not the patron, except as a gloss below; s 23(2)(i), (ia) and (2a) (officers and casino employees who play);
-- s 32 (detention of suspected offenders -- the deposit omits the Table of provisions it applies to); s 15 (unclaimed
-- winnings); s 30 and s 31 (cheating, forgery); s 23(4) (suing for winnings or gaming loans). Machinery out: Parts II-VA
-- (the Commission's staff, the casino complex agreement, licensing, the Independent Monitor), s 36, s 37, Part 7.
-- Infringement procedure (Criminal Procedure Act 2004 Part 2; the 28 days in Schedule 2 Form 1) is out.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Casino Control Act 1984 -- the patron's questions`

§§ `s 26 -- who may ban me`

-- s 26(1): "A person does not have a right against the owner or occupier of a licensed casino, or a casino licensee, to
-- enter or remain in the licensed casino, except by the licence of that occupier, owner or casino licensee."
-- (1a): "A person authorised by the casino licensee ... may, either orally or in writing, prohibit a person from entering or
-- remaining in the licensed casino." (2): "The casino licensee concerned or some person acting under the licensee's
-- authority or the Commissioner of Police may give to a person a direction in writing prohibiting the person from entering
-- or remaining in the licensed casino."
-- No provision lets a member of the patron's family, or the patron, apply for a ban, and no provision gives the Commission
-- (the Gaming and Wagering Commission, s 3(1)) power to ban; s 26A lets it confirm or revoke a casino's direction.
DECLARE `Who wants me kept out` IS ONE OF
    `the casino`                                 -- the casino licensee or a person acting under its authority
    `the Commissioner of Police`
    `the Gaming and Wagering Commission`         -- "the Commission", s 3(1)
    `a member of my family`
    `I myself`

DECLARE `What the Act lets them do` IS ONE OF
    `ban me on the spot for up to 24 hours (s 26(1a)), or by written direction until the casino revokes it (s 26(2))`
    `ban me by written direction, in force once the casino is told of it in writing (s 26(2), (3))`
    `not ban me, but confirm or revoke a casino direction if I apply for review (s 26A)`
    `nothing: the Act gives my family no power to ban me and no right to apply for a ban`
    `nothing of my own: the Act has no self-exclusion, so a ban on me is the casino or the Commissioner of Police giving one`

@export Who can keep me out of a WA casino, and how (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 26, 26A)?
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who wants me kept out` @desc Who wants you kept out of the casino
GIVETH A `What the Act lets them do`
DECIDE `What can this person do to keep me out of the casino` IS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the casino` THEN `ban me on the spot for up to 24 hours (s 26(1a)), or by written direction until the casino revokes it (s 26(2))`
    WHEN `the Commissioner of Police` THEN `ban me by written direction, in force once the casino is told of it in writing (s 26(2), (3))`
    WHEN `the Gaming and Wagering Commission` THEN `not ban me, but confirm or revoke a casino direction if I apply for review (s 26A)`
    WHEN `a member of my family` THEN `nothing: the Act gives my family no power to ban me and no right to apply for a ban`
    WHEN `I myself` THEN `nothing of my own: the Act has no self-exclusion, so a ban on me is the casino or the Commissioner of Police giving one`

@export May a member of my family apply to have me banned from a WA casino (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 26)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my family apply to have me banned` IS FALSE

@export Have I a right to enter or stay in a WA casino against the casino's wishes (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 26(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I a right to enter the casino` IS FALSE

§§ `s 26(1b), (3), (4), 26A(5) -- is the ban on me in force`

-- (1b): a prohibition under (1a) "remains in force -- (a) for a period of 24 hours from the time at which it was so made; or
-- (b) until it is revoked ... whichever is the sooner."
-- (3): a direction "by the Commissioner of Police is of no effect until notice has been given in writing of that direction
-- to the casino licensee concerned."
-- (4): a casino's direction "remains in force until it is revoked -- (i) by that casino licensee; or (ii) by a determination
-- of the Commission under section 26A(5)"; the Commissioner's "remains in force until it is revoked by him and that
-- revocation is notified in writing to the casino licensee concerned."
-- A casino direction has no time limit in the text: it lasts until revoked.
DECLARE `Who banned me` IS ONE OF
    `nobody`
    `the casino on the spot`                            -- s 26(1a): orally or in writing, by a person the casino authorised
    `the casino by written direction`                   -- s 26(2)
    `the Commissioner of Police by written direction`   -- s 26(2), (3)

DECLARE `My ban` HAS
    `who banned me`                                       IS A `Who banned me`
    `hours since the ban was made`                        IS A NUMBER
    `the person who made it has revoked it`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission has revoked it on review and given notice` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 26A(5)(b)
    `the casino has been given written notice of the ban` IS A BOOLEAN        -- s 26(3), police directions only
    `the casino has been given written notice of the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 26(4)(b), police directions only

`the hours an on-the-spot ban lasts at most` MEANS 24

@export Is the ban on me in force (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 26(1b), (3), (4), s 26A(5))?
GIVEN `the ban` IS A `My ban` @desc Who banned you, how long ago, and whether it has been revoked or notified
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the ban on me in force` IF
    CONSIDER `the ban`'s `who banned me`
    WHEN `nobody` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the casino on the spot` THEN
            `the ban`'s `hours since the ban was made` LESS THAN `the hours an on-the-spot ban lasts at most`
        AND (NOT `the ban`'s `the person who made it has revoked it`)
    WHEN `the casino by written direction` THEN
            (NOT `the ban`'s `the person who made it has revoked it`)
        AND (NOT `the ban`'s `the Commission has revoked it on review and given notice`)
    WHEN `the Commissioner of Police by written direction` THEN
            `the ban`'s `the casino has been given written notice of the ban`
        AND (NOT (    `the ban`'s `the person who made it has revoked it`
                  AND `the ban`'s `the casino has been given written notice of the revocation`))

§§ `s 26A, r 4 -- may I have the ban reviewed`

-- s 26A(1): "A person ... who is given a direction under section 26(2) by the casino licensee concerned or a person acting
-- under the licensee's authority may apply to the Commission to review the direction." (2): it "remains in force during
-- the period of the review." (3): in writing with grounds, "accompanied by the prescribed fee". (5): the Commission
-- confirms or revokes, and notifies the applicant and the casino.
-- Casino Control Regulations 1999 r 4: "For the purposes of section 26A(3)(b) of the Act, the prescribed fee is $179."
-- No review is given of an on-the-spot prohibition (it lapses in 24 hours) or of a Commissioner of Police direction.
@export May I apply to the Gaming and Wagering Commission to review the ban on me (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 26A(1))?
GIVEN `the ban` IS A `My ban` @desc Who banned you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to have my ban reviewed` IF
    `the ban`'s `who banned me` EQUALS `the casino by written direction`

@export What fee must I pay to have a casino ban reviewed, in dollars (Casino Control Regulations 1999 r 4)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fee must I pay for a review` IS 179

@export Does the ban stay in force while the Commission reviews it (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 26A(2))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my ban stay in force during the review` IS TRUE

§§ `ss 23, 26, 27, 27A and Schedule 1 -- the offences a patron can commit`

-- The patron's offences, each with the court maximum in the Act and the modified penalty an infringement notice may offer
-- (Casino Control Regulations 1999 r 8, Schedule 1 Division 1).
--   s 26(1d) entering or remaining while an on-the-spot prohibition is in force: "a fine of $5 000"; item 4: $500.
--   s 26(6) entering or remaining while a written direction is in force: "a fine of $10 000"; item 5: $1 000.
--   s 23(2)(ii) a person "in respect of whom a prohibition or direction under section 26 is in force" who "participates as a
--     player in any game in the casino": "a fine of $50 000"; item 3: $500.
--   s 27(3) a person under 18 entering or remaining, unless s 27(4) applies: "(a) for a first offence, a fine of $1 000; (b)
--     for a second or subsequent offence, a fine of $2 000"; item 8: $200.
--   s 27(3a) a person under 18 participating in gaming: "a fine of $2 000"; item 9: $200.
--   s 27A(4) a false statement of age, or failing without reasonable excuse to leave when required: "a fine of $2 000";
--     item 10: $200.
-- No imprisonment is provided for any of them.
DECLARE `Patron offence` IS ONE OF
    `entering or staying under an on-the-spot ban (s 26(1d))`
    `entering or staying under a written direction (s 26(6))`
    `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))`
    `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))`
    `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))`
    `a false age or not leaving when required (s 27A(4))`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for this casino offence, in dollars (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 23(2), 26(1d), (6), 27(3), (3a), 27A(4))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Patron offence` @desc The offence
      `I have been convicted of it before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this would be a second or later offence (matters only under s 27(3))
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `entering or staying under an on-the-spot ban (s 26(1d))` THEN 5000
    WHEN `entering or staying under a written direction (s 26(6))` THEN 10000
    WHEN `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))` THEN 50000
    WHEN `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` THEN IF `I have been convicted of it before` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `a false age or not leaving when required (s 27A(4))` THEN 2000

@export What would an infringement notice ask me to pay for this casino offence, in dollars (Casino Control Regulations 1999 r 8 and Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Patron offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What would an infringement notice ask me to pay` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `entering or staying under an on-the-spot ban (s 26(1d))` THEN 500
    WHEN `entering or staying under a written direction (s 26(6))` THEN 1000
    WHEN `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))` THEN 500
    WHEN `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` THEN 200
    WHEN `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` THEN 200
    WHEN `a false age or not leaving when required (s 27A(4))` THEN 200

-- s 23(2b) and s 27(3b): on conviction "the court shall, on the application of the prosecutor and in addition to any other
-- penalty ... order the forfeiture to the Crown of any winnings paid to the person as a result of the commission of the
-- offence." The prosecutor's application is the prosecutor's choice, so it is asked.
@export If I am convicted, must the court take my winnings (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 23(2b), 27(3b))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Patron offence` @desc The offence you were convicted of
      `the prosecutor applies for forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the prosecutor applies for your winnings to be forfeited
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my winnings be forfeited` IF
        `the prosecutor applies for forfeiture`
    AND (   `the offence` EQUALS `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))`
         OR `the offence` EQUALS `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))`)

§§ `ss 22, 23, 26, 27 -- my visit`

-- s 27(4): a person under 18 may enter or remain "for the purposes only of -- (a) employment in connection with the provision
-- of amenities ancillary to the gaming therein; or (b) obtaining a meal, if that person is accompanied by another person who
-- is over the age of 18 years and is -- (i) the spouse or parent of; or (ii) a person in loco parentis to; or (iii) the
-- guardian of, the person under the age of 18 years, and the person under the age of 18 years does not participate in
-- gaming".
-- s 22(1)(a): the Commission may declare "any game, except for a game played with poker machines, to be an authorised game".
-- s 23(1)(b): "the playing of an authorised game in accordance with the approved rules ... shall be taken not to be
-- prohibited and, except in so far as subsection (2) applies, is not unlawful."
DECLARE `Why I am there` IS ONE OF
    `to gamble or for anything else`
    `to work in the amenities ancillary to the gaming`   -- s 27(4)(a)
    `to have a meal`                                     -- s 27(4)(b)

DECLARE `Kind of game` IS ONE OF
    `no game`
    `an authorised game`                 -- declared by the Commission under s 22(1), rules approved under s 22(2)
    `a game not declared authorised`
    `a game played with a poker machine` -- s 22(1)(a): cannot be declared authorised

DECLARE `My visit` HAS
    `my age in years`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `why I am there`                                        IS A `Why I am there`
    `with my spouse, parent or guardian who is over 18`     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 27(4)(b)(i)-(iii), in loco parentis included
    `I play`                                                IS A BOOLEAN   -- "participates as a player" (s 23(2)); "participate in gaming" (s 27)
    `the game`                                              IS A `Kind of game`
    `it is played to the approved rules`                    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `v` IS A `My visit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am under 18` IF `v`'s `my age in years` LESS THAN 18

@export Does s 27(4) let me into a WA casino although I am under 18 (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 27(4))?
GIVEN `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc Your age, why you are there, who is with you, and whether you play
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 27(4) let me in although I am under 18` IF
        `I am under 18` `the visit`
    AND (NOT `the visit`'s `I play`)
    AND CONSIDER `the visit`'s `why I am there`
        WHEN `to work in the amenities ancillary to the gaming` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to have a meal` THEN `the visit`'s `with my spouse, parent or guardian who is over 18`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Is it an offence for me to enter or stay in the casino (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 26(1d), (6), 27(3))?
GIVEN `the ban` IS A `My ban` @desc Any ban on you
      `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc Your age, why you are there, who is with you, and whether you play
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay` IF
        `Is the ban on me in force` `the ban`
    OR  (`I am under 18` `the visit` AND (NOT `Does s 27(4) let me in although I am under 18` `the visit`))

@export Is it an offence for me to play in the casino (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 23(2)(ii), 27(3a))?
GIVEN `the ban` IS A `My ban` @desc Any ban on you
      `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc Your age and whether you play
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it an offence for me to play` IF
        `the visit`'s `I play`
    AND (`Is the ban on me in force` `the ban` OR `I am under 18` `the visit`)

-- s 23(2), s 26(1d), (6) and s 27(3), (3a) are separate offences; this gives the largest single maximum among those the
-- visit commits, 0 if none.
@export What is the largest fine I risk for this visit, in dollars (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 23(2), 26(1d), (6), 27(3), (3a))?
GIVEN `the ban` IS A `My ban` @desc Any ban on you
      `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc Your age, why you are there, who is with you, and whether you play
      `I have been convicted under s 27(3) before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted before of being in a casino under 18
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest fine I risk for this visit` IS
    BRANCH
      IF `Is the ban on me in force` `the ban` AND `the visit`'s `I play`
        THEN `What is the most I can be fined for` `playing while banned (s 23(2)(ii))` FALSE
      IF `Is the ban on me in force` `the ban` AND `the ban`'s `who banned me` EQUALS `the casino on the spot`
        THEN `What is the most I can be fined for` `entering or staying under an on-the-spot ban (s 26(1d))` FALSE
      IF `Is the ban on me in force` `the ban`
        THEN `What is the most I can be fined for` `entering or staying under a written direction (s 26(6))` FALSE
      IF `I am under 18` `the visit` AND `the visit`'s `I play`
        THEN `What is the most I can be fined for` `gaming under 18 (s 27(3a))` FALSE
      IF `Is it an offence for me to enter or stay` `the ban` `the visit`
        THEN `What is the most I can be fined for` `entering or staying under 18 (s 27(3))` `I have been convicted under s 27(3) before`
      OTHERWISE 0

@export Is the game I am playing lawful in the casino (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 22(1), 23(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc The game you play and whether it is played to the approved rules
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the game lawful in the casino` IF
        `the visit`'s `the game` EQUALS `an authorised game`
    AND `the visit`'s `it is played to the approved rules`

§§ `ss 26(1c), (5), 27A -- may I be removed by force`

-- s 26(1c), (5): while a prohibition or direction "remains in force, a person authorised ... may with the use of reasonable
-- force exclude or remove the person who is the subject of" it.
-- s 27A(1): if an authorised person "suspects on reasonable grounds" that a person (not one to whom s 27(4) applies) is under
-- 18, they may require the person to state their age; (2) if "the stated age appears to the authorised person to be false",
-- they may require evidence of age or, if the person "is unable or refuses to produce such evidence, to leave"; (3) one who
-- does not leave may be removed "with the use of reasonable force". (5): authorised person means the casino or a person
-- acting under its authority, an officer of the Commission, or a member of the Police Force.
-- The suspicion and the appearance of falsity are the authorised person's judgments, so they are asked.
DECLARE `Age check` HAS
    `an authorised person suspected on reasonable grounds that I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my stated age appeared false to them`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I produced evidence of my age`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I left when required`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had a reasonable excuse for not leaving`                              IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `v` IS A `My visit`
      `c` IS A `Age check`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I may be required to leave for want of proof of age` IF
        (NOT `Does s 27(4) let me in although I am under 18` `v`)
    AND `c`'s `an authorised person suspected on reasonable grounds that I am under 18`
    AND `c`'s `my stated age appeared false to them`
    AND (NOT `c`'s `I produced evidence of my age`)

@export May I be removed from the casino with reasonable force (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) ss 26(1c), (5), 27A(3))?
GIVEN `the ban` IS A `My ban` @desc Any ban on you
      `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc Your age and why you are there
      `the check` IS A `Age check` @desc Whether you were asked your age, and what happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be removed with reasonable force` IF
        `Is the ban on me in force` `the ban`
    OR  (`I may be required to leave for want of proof of age` `the visit` `the check` AND (NOT `the check`'s `I left when required`))

@export Have I committed the offence of not leaving when I could not prove my age (Casino Control Act 1984 (WA) s 27A(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the visit` IS A `My visit` @desc Your age and why you are there
      `the check` IS A `Age check` @desc Whether you were asked your age, and what happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed the offence of not leaving` IF
        `I may be required to leave for want of proof of age` `the visit` `the check`
    AND (NOT `the check`'s `I left when required`)
    AND (NOT `the check`'s `I had a reasonable excuse for not leaving`)
